---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import aboutHero from '../assets/about-hero.jpg';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Why this blog exists and how a post gets written."
		/>
		<style>
			main {
				width: calc(100% - 2em);
				max-width: 100%;
				margin: 0;
				padding: 2em 1em 3em;
			}
			.hero-image {
				width: 100%;
			}
			.hero-image img {
				display: block;
				margin: 0 auto;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 8px;
				box-shadow: var(--box-shadow);
			}
			.prose {
				width: 720px;
				max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
				margin: auto;
				padding: 1em;
				color: var(--text);
			}
			.title {
				margin-bottom: 1.5em;
				padding: 1em 0 0;
			}
			.title h1 {
				margin: 0 0 0.6em 0;
				font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.8rem);
				line-height: 1.15;
			}
			.rule {
				width: 56px;
				height: 3px;
				margin-bottom: 1.5em;
				background: var(--brand-yellow);
			}
			.prose h2 {
				margin: 2em 0 0.75em 0;
				font-size: 1.4rem;
			}
			.prose p {
				line-height: 1.7;
			}
			.prose ol {
				line-height: 1.8;
				padding-left: 1.25em;
			}
			.prose ol li {
				margin-bottom: 0.5em;
			}
			.not-list p {
				margin: 0 0 0.4em 0;
			}
			.closing {
				margin-top: 2em;
				padding-top: 1.5em;
				border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
				color: rgb(var(--muted-rgb));
			}
		</style>
	</head>

	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<article>
				<div class="hero-image">
					<Image width={1020} height={510} src={aboutHero} alt="" />
				</div>
				<div class="prose">
					<div class="title">
						<h1>Why this page exists</h1>
						<div class="rule"></div>
					</div>

					<p>
						Most people first meet AO on Twitter, Discord, or a short post. By the time they get
						here, they have usually already seen fragments of the same idea repeated in different
						lengths. This page is where those fragments come from.
					</p>

					<h2>How a post gets written</h2>
					<ol>
						<li>Someone asks a real question in public.</li>
						<li>
							We research it against our own trade records, the public dashboard, and whatever
							external data is relevant.
						</li>
						<li>We write the full answer, the surface question and the resistance underneath it.</li>
						<li>That answer gets published here.</li>
						<li>Compressed versions go out to the platforms where the original question was asked.</li>
					</ol>
					<p>
						If the research does not support a claim, it does not go in. If a loss is part of the
						answer, the loss goes in with the same weight as a win.
					</p>

					<h2>What this is not</h2>
					<div class="not-list">
						<p>It is not a daily market commentary feed.</p>
						<p>It is not a place to restate what we already said on social.</p>
						<p>It is not content written to fill a calendar.</p>
					</div>
					<p>
						It is the place where the thinking happens in full view, so that every shorter piece of
						content can stay short without becoming thin.
					</p>

					<p class="closing">
						You can read the posts without joining anything. The questions are public. The answers
						are public. The trade record they rest on is public. That is the point.
					</p>
				</div>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>